\f1\b\fs36 \cf0 1. Interpretation\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\fs24 \cf0 The overall shape:
\f0\b0 \strokec2  This is a fundamentally prosocial, principled leadership profile. Your "dark tetrad" scores (narcissism, Machiavellianism, psychopathy, sadism) are all average or below, except for one \'97 Machiavellianism \'97 which sits moderately elevated. Your empathy, humility, and ethical leadership scores are all comfortably above average, with humility and ethical leadership notably high. Psychopathy being low is important: it means the Machiavellian streak is probably not cold or callous \'97 it's paired with real empathy, so it likely shows up as 
\f2\i \strokec2 strategic thinking
\f0\i0 \strokec2  rather than 
\f2\i \strokec2 exploitation
\f0\i0 \strokec2 .\

\f1\b \strokec2 What the Machiavellianism score likely means in practice:
\f0\b0 \strokec2  People in the moderate-high range on this trait tend to:\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls1\ilvl0\cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Think several moves ahead in organizational politics, and plan communication carefully rather than saying whatever comes to mind\
\ls1\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Feel comfortable with ambiguity, calculated risk, and negotiation\
\ls1\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Sometimes hold information back "strategically" rather than sharing by default\
\ls1\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 View relationships partly through a lens of what they enable, especially under pressure\
\ls1\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Feel mildly cynical about others' motives ("what's the angle here?") even when nothing is wrong\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \strokec2 Because your empathy and ethics scores are high, this strategic instinct is probably 
\f2\i \strokec2 checked
\f0\i0 \strokec2  most of the time. But it's the trait most likely to create a gap between your intentions and how others experience you \'97 because strategic communication, even well-meant, can read to others as guarded, political, or hard to fully trust.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b \cf0 \strokec2 Biases to watch for:
\f0\b0 \strokec2 \
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls2\ilvl0
\f1\b \cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Ends-justify-means creep
\f0\b0  \'97 the ethical-leadership score is a strong anchor, but it's tested most under time pressure or high stakes, not in calm moments. That's when a moderate Machiavellian streak is most likely to nudge a decision.\
\ls2\ilvl0
\f1\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Assuming others are more calculating than they are
\f0\b0  \'97 moderate Machiavellianism often comes with a bias toward reading hidden motives into neutral behavior.\
\ls2\ilvl0
\f1\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Under-selling yourself
\f0\b0  \'97 high humility is a strength, but it can tip into reflexively deflecting credit or not advocating for your own ideas, which costs you influence and sometimes lets less careful voices shape decisions.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

