\f0\b0 \strokec2  Once a day, notice one moment where you'd normally deflect credit or downplay your contribution, and instead state it plainly and briefly ("I led that redesign" instead of "the team did a great job").\

\f1\b \strokec2 Workplace behavior:
\f0\b0 \strokec2  In one setting (1:1, team meeting, or written update), advocate directly for something you or your team needs, without softening it into a suggestion.\

\f1\b \strokec2 Reflection questions:
