\f1\b\fs36 \cf0 5. Scripts\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\fs24 \cf0 Seeking feedback:
\f0\b0 \strokec2 \
"I'm working on being more transparent about my reasoning and better at giving credit where it's due. Can you tell me about a specific moment recently where my communication either worked well or left you unsure where I stood?"\

\f1\b \strokec2 Pausing before a reactive decision:
\f0\b0 \strokec2 \
"I want to give this a real answer, not a fast one \'97 let me take [an hour / until tomorrow] and come back to you." 
\f2\i \strokec2 (Internal version: "What's the principle here, not just the outcome I want?")
\f0\i0 \strokec2 \

\f1\b \strokec2 Giving credit:
\f0\b0 \strokec2 \
"I want to be specific: [Name] did the actual work on this \'97 the idea and execution were theirs. I want that visible, not folded into 'the team.'"\

\f1\b \strokec2 Repairing harm:
\f0\b0 \strokec2 \
"I think my decision/comment about [X] landed harder than I meant it to, and I want to understand your side of it before I explain mine. What did it feel like from where you sat?"\

\f1\b \strokec2 Responding to conflict:
\f0\b0 \strokec2 \
"I think we want the same outcome here and disagree on the path. Can we name what we're each optimizing for, so we're arguing about the actual tradeoff instead of past each other?"\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \strokec2 \
